You can bypass both problems just by obsessively
cutting and pasting every article you write to and
from a decent plain text editor. I like vim(), from
http://www.vim.org, because it knows how to do
useful things for news article authoring like
reflowing paragraphs of text quoted with Usenet
standard right angle brackets, but your favorite
plain text editor with a fixed pitch font will
probably work perfectly well for you.

The few extra keystrokes to do the cut and paste (I
keep a copy of vim() open for this use at all times,
might be editing five news articles at once in it)
are hundredsfold repaid by the frustration saved in
making a really pretty and readable posting.

